From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:37:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 78/99] v8: wasm code reference scopes: TLS model of V8,
 nothing to drop when empty

Every stack walk of an isolate opens a WasmCodeRefScope, the walks of a
JS throw too. Its thread-local pointer had no TLS model, so code built
with -fPIC used the general dynamic one; the e2k GNU linker does not
relax it, and every access was a call of __tls_get_addr (about 40 cycles
more than a local-exec load, measured on Elbrus-8SV). It now takes
V8_TLS_MODEL like the isolate pointer. The destructor of a scope that
took no reference (all walks without wasm frames) no longer builds the
dead code tables of DecrementRefCount.

bench.js tryCatch on Elbrus-8SV: 943 -> 916 ms (s8e without wasm: 845).
---
 chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc b/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
index dbfcfa9ef3..b0374e4e21 100644
--- a/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
+++ b/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "src/codegen/macro-assembler.h"
 #include "src/common/code-memory-access.h"
 #include "src/common/globals.h"
+#include "src/common/thread-local-storage.h"
 #include "src/deoptimizer/deoptimizer.h"
 #include "src/diagnostics/disassembler.h"
 #include "src/logging/counters.h"
@@ -3119,7 +3120,12 @@ void WasmCodeManager::FlushCodeLookupCache(Isolate* isolate) {
 }
 
 namespace {
-thread_local WasmCodeRefScope* current_code_refs_scope = nullptr;
+// Every stack walk of the isolate opens a scope, the walk for a JS exception
+// too. Without the model the compiler takes the general dynamic one, and
+// where the linker does not relax it (GNU ld for e2k) each access is a call
+// of __tls_get_addr.
+__attribute__((tls_model(V8_TLS_MODEL))) thread_local WasmCodeRefScope*
+    current_code_refs_scope = nullptr;
 }  // namespace
 
 WasmCodeRefScope::WasmCodeRefScope()
@@ -3130,6 +3136,9 @@ WasmCodeRefScope::WasmCodeRefScope()
 WasmCodeRefScope::~WasmCodeRefScope() {
   DCHECK_EQ(this, current_code_refs_scope);
   current_code_refs_scope = previous_scope_;
+  // Most scopes (all of those of stack walks without wasm frames) took no
+  // reference.
+  if (code_ptrs_.empty()) return;
   WasmCode::DecrementRefCount(base::VectorOf(code_ptrs_));
 }
 
